installer-url-contains-forbidden-fragment = URL contains forbidden fragment: { $arg1 }
installer-url-contains-forbidden-userinfo = URL contains forbidden userinfo: { $arg1 }
installer-usage = usage: { $arg1 }
installer-variant-for-on-is-missing-in-manifest = Variant { $arg1 } for { $arg2 } on { $arg3 } is missing in manifest
installer-verify-and-preview-without-changing-the-installation = verify and preview without changing the installation
installer-verify-the-journal-installation-before-removing-it = Verify the Journal installation before removing it.
installer-was-found = was found
installer-was-not-found = was not found
installer-was-not-moved-into-place = { $arg1 } was not moved into place
installer-without-a-selection-an-interactive-terminal-shows = without a selection, an interactive terminal shows the component menu.
installer-without-this-installer-s-record-so-this = without this installer's record, so this installer will not change it. Nothing was changed.
installer-your-journal-and-the-solstone-app-update = your journal and the solstone app update themselves: once a day they check for a new version and install it in the background. your journal never restarts on its own; the new version starts the next time it does. to turn this off: { $arg1 }
installer-your-journal-now-updates-with-this-installer = your journal now updates with this installer, from where it is: { $arg1 }
installer-your-journal-updates-itself-once-a-day = your journal updates itself: once a day it checks for a new version and installs it in the background. the new version starts the next time your journal does. to turn this off: { $arg1 }
installer-your-journal-was-updated-where-it-is = { $arg1 }. Your journal was updated where it is, in { $arg2 }, but this installer did not take it over. Once the problem above is fixed, run the same { $arg3 } command again.
installer-your-package-manager = your package manager

installer-journal-viewer-dependencies = your journal will open in your browser. to install the desktop libraries for its own window, run { $arg1 }.
installer-journal-viewer-system-package = your journal will open in your browser. to use the journal window on this computer, install the solstone desktop system package with its AppArmor profile.
